// expect: 7
// mn-lambda-list-param — a list pattern with a rest as a function
// literal's parameter (PLAN §11 Phase 3.3's first measured drift). It was
// authored as the binder form, whose paren content parses as an EXPRESSION
// first, so the list parser mints the rest as a cover-grammar node
// (RestExpr) that expr_to_pat consumes; `mentl fmt` writes a sole-parameter
// literal as its arm list, so the canonical page holds the pattern as an
// arm, and both spellings are one graph. The frontier leg gates both
// halves: zero diagnostics at check, and the program runs to 7 — the rest
// binding is the list runtime's slice, reached like any other call.
fn pick(f, xs) = f(xs)

fn main(q) = pick({ [h, ...t] => h }, [7, 8, 9])
